  {
    "id": "628c4e7b-9d3d-3187-a0cd-fe1dedc56e42",
    "content": {
      "id": "628c4e7b-9d3d-3187-a0cd-fe1dedc56e42",
      "contentType": "STORY",
      "title": "Ignoring AI bubble fears, investors bet Nvidia and Google will fuel Taiwan stocks to record",
      "description": "",
      "summary": "Taiwan's tech-heavy stocks show few signs of slowing a rally even as AI bubble worries cast a shadow over global markets, underscoring home-grown confidence in the structural advantages in AI that foreign investors may have overlooked.  Taiwan's benchmark index is poised to breach ​a record 30,000 points in 2026, investors say, extending a three-year surge that has seen the stock market nearly double as the island rides a wave of demand ‌for chips that power artificial intelligence.  While foreign money worries about stretched AI valuations, Taiwanese investors have enthusiastically ploughed into the market.",
      "pubDate": "2025-12-12T05:31:50Z",
      "displayTime": "2025-12-12T05:31:50Z",
      "isHosted": true,
      "bypassModal": false,
      "previewUrl": null,
      "thumbnail": {
        "originalUrl": "https://media.zenfs.com/en/reuters-finance.com/1303e6d6fc5d27d84e672269b5c5eb00",
        "originalWidth": 800,
        "originalHeight": 533,
        "caption": "FILE PHOTO: Illustration shows NVIDIA logo",
